.TH AUDIOCONTROL\-METADATA 1 "September 2026" "AudioControl Manual" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
audiocontrol\-metadata \- HiFiBerry audio control metadata daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B audiocontrol\-metadata
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B audiocontrol\-metadata
is the second of the two daemons in this package. It owns everything that
reaches outside the device: MusicBrainz, TheAudioDB and fanart.tv lookups,
cover art, artist images, favourites and Last.fm now\-playing and scrobbling.
.PP
It listens on loopback port 1084 and is not reachable from the network; nginx
forwards the metadata prefixes to it. Every connection between the two daemons
is opened by this one, so it needs the player daemon's API root in its
configuration and the player daemon holds no address for it.
.PP
It does not need the player daemon to be running in order to start. On
start\-up it polls the player daemon's
.I /api/version
for up to 30 seconds and then starts regardless, leaving its subscriber to
reconnect. While the player daemon is unavailable, enrichment results are
dropped and playback is unaffected; while this daemon is unavailable, playback,
volume, the library and the WebSocket all keep working, and there is no
enrichment, no cover art and no scrobbling.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c " " \fIFILE\fR
Use the specified configuration file instead of the default
.IR metadata.json .
The packaged unit passes
.IR /etc/audiocontrol/metadata.json .
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-debug
Log everything at debug level.
.TP
.B \-\-check\-secrets
Report which API credentials are compiled into this binary, without printing
their values, and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information and exit.
.SH LOGGING
This daemon logs to standard error, which
.BR systemd (1)
records in the journal; see
.BR journalctl (1)
.RB "with " "\-u audiocontrol\-metadata" .
The level defaults to
.I info
and is set with the
.B RUST_LOG
environment variable, or with
.B \-\-debug
for everything at debug level.
.PP
It does
.B not
read
.IR /etc/audiocontrol/logging.json .
That file configures the player daemon only, and its per\-subsystem levels and
file logging have no equivalent here yet. Passing
.B \-\-log\-config
is reported as ignored rather than silently accepted.
.SH CONFIGURATION
The configuration file must name the player daemon's API root:
.PP
.RS
"core": { "url": "http://127.0.0.1:1080/api" }
.RE
.PP
The daemon refuses to start without it, deliberately. It is not derived from
.IR services.webserver.port ,
which is this daemon's own port: a derived value would make the daemon
subscribe to its own event stream and poll its own library, neither of which it
serves, and it would fail silently rather than at start\-up.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/audiocontrol/metadata.json
Default configuration file. Distinct from
.IR audiocontrol.json ,
which configures the player daemon; the two share several section names and are
not interchangeable.
.TP
.I /var/lib/audiocontrol/metadata/
This daemon's own state: its lookup cache, its settings database, its image
cache and its credential store. Separate from the player daemon's, because two
processes writing one SQLite file or one credential store would lose data.
.TP
.I /etc/hifiberry/auth.d/audiocontrol\-metadata\-auth.json
Which of its routes the API gateway treats as ordinary and which as privileged.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR audiocontrol (1),
.BR audiocontrol_dump_cache (1),
.BR audiocontrol_dump_store (1),
.BR audiocontrol_favourites (1),
.BR audiocontrol_musicbrainz_client (1)
